=== layout: section

# Grading and Assessment

=== layout: one-panel

# Assignments, Quizzes, and Exams

@body

- [*Assignments*]{color=red}: reinforce learning; explore new topics
  - Weekly; 5-15 points; unlimited retakes
  - Collaboration and help encouraged
- [*Quizzes*]{color=red}: recent material
  - Individual: 20 points; 30 minutes
  - Group quiz during class
- [*Exams*]{color=red}: cumulative midterm and final
  - Individual; 100 points total
  - Each part: 50 points; 75 minutes

=== layout: two-panels

# Graded vs Total Percentage

@left

- *Graded percentage* includes only items with a recorded grade.
- Excludes items that have not been graded, including unfinished assignments.
- More useful when *Dr. Voss* still has submitted work to grade.

@right

- *Total percentage* includes all items counted toward your Blackboard grade.
- Counts items without a recorded grade as zero.
  - This includes submitted work waiting to be graded.
- More useful for seeing the effect of assignments you have not attempted.

=== layout: section

# Quiz/Exam

=== layout: one-panel

# [Don&rsquo;t Panic]{color=red}

@body

- If you experience internet troubles or non-academic distractions during a quiz/exam\:
  - 1. Don&rsquo;t panic
  - 2. Stop and close the quiz/exam without looking at all the questions
  - 3. [Contact me immediately]{color=red}, preferably via Discord, but you do not need to rush
- Note\: Once class begins, I no longer check my email.
- If you haven't looked at all the questions, I can reset the quiz/exam
- If you have looked at some questions, I can create a new custom quiz/exam with only the portion that you haven't seen yet.

=== layout: one-panel

# Illness Policy

@body

- Since COVID, I am trying to be more considerate of student illnesses.
- If you are sick, let me know. I will provide an extension.
- If a major event interferes (car accident, etc.), again contact me.
- Communication is always helpful.

=== layout: section

# Quiz

=== layout: two-panels

# Quiz System Information

@left

- 20 points; 18-24 questions
- MC: 1 point; matching: 1/2 per choice
- 30 minutes; about 1.5 min/question
- Backtracking allowed; random order
- Limited calculations
- Score: (individual + group)/2
- Example: (14 + 20)/2 = 17

@right

- Individual: Blackboard
- Opens >20 hours before class
- Due BEFORE class
- Group: Zoom and Blackboard
- 3-4 students; breakout setup takes time
- Hard group quizzes receive a curve

=== layout: one-panel

# Missing Group Quizzes

@body

- Make-up quizzes will be allowed for full credit only if the student notifies the instructor BEFORE the quiz/exam
- Students missing group quizzes cannot later work in a group
  - the individual score will be averaged with the minimum 18 points (or higher) instead of a group quiz score
  - so you still get the benefit of the group score average, albeit small, even though you missed the in-class quiz.

=== layout: one-panel

# Please Volunteer Only If Plan to Work in Group

@body

- You get Group Quiz points no matter what.
  - your individual score will be averaged with the standard 18 points (sometimes higher) instead of a group quiz score
- Group Quiz is not required.
- Do not join if you do not want to actively participate.
- Let me know if you want to work with someone in particular.

=== layout: one-panel

# Group Quiz Setup

@body

- Complete your individual quiz FIRST
- Before: join your assigned breakout group
  - Select a Recorder to share their screen
  - ONLY the Recorder starts the unique Blackboard quiz
- During: 30 minutes; enter your first names
  - Discuss verbally or in chat
  - Use Ask for Help for instructor assistance
- After: review correct and submitted answers
  - Report problems by email or Discord DM
  - Return to main room or stay and chat

=== layout: one-panel

# Low Quiz Grades

@body

- How can I do better in this class?
- Did you complete the relevant assignments before taking the quiz?
  - The assignments and quizzes mostly have the same questions.
- Did you retake the relevant assignments and make sure you understood the questions? Did you retake them until you had a grade you were happy with?
  - The assignments and quizzes mostly have the same questions.

